      "content": "interesting. so you're saying the legal arguments are basically just invalid? what about the philosophical argument regarding individual liberty—the idea that it's fundamentally unjust to penalize one group of citizens to satisfy a debt they didn't personally incur? is there any way that can be viewed as a legitimate ethical position rather than just a calculation to protect the status quo?",
